      "text": [
        " : \"اَلْمَيِّتُ أَحَقُّ بِمَالِهِ مَا دَامَ فِيهِ اَلرُّوحُ يُبِينُ بِهِ\" قَالَ \"فَإِنْ تَعَدَّى فَلَيْسَ لَهُ إِلاَّ اَلثُّلُثُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5426 - Ibn Abi Umayr narrated from Murazim from Ammar Al-Sabaṭi from Abu Abdullah Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as), who said:\n\"The deceased has the most right over his wealth as long as his soul remains in him and he can express himself.\"\nImam (as) then said: \"But if he exceeds (in his bequest), he is entitled only to one-third.\""
        ]
      }
